function: DQM queue IRQ-status service helper for CP2/FPM event groups.

Behavior:
  - reads {@symbol b6001818}
  - services DQM queue pending groups:
      0x00200000:
        drains CP2 e004/e005/e006-side event/token data while
        {@symbol 8000800c}
        still carries bit 0x00200000
        returns values to {@symbol b2200200}
        or reinjects through CP2 e000/e001
        acks 0x00200000 back to {@symbol b6001818}

      0x0000ff00:
        iterates selector indexes 15..8 through CP2 selector register 0x806
        drains CP2 f000/f001 word pairs into the DQM mode/window area
        acks 0x0000ff00 back to {@symbol b6001818}

      0x00400000:
        drains CP2 e804/e805/e806-side event data
        either returns token/data to {@symbol b2200200}
        or writes a DQM mode/window entry
        acks 0x00400000 back to {@symbol b6001818}

      0x02000000:
        drains CP2 e800 command/event word
        emits command 0xdd or 0xdc through:
          {@symbol DQM_COMMAND_WORD_16001D20_candidate}
          {@symbol DQM_COMMAND_ARG_WORD_16001D24_candidate}
        acks 0x02000000 back to {@symbol b6001818}

Current interpretation:
  DQM-internal CP2/FPM queue service routine called from the DQM IRQ/mailbox
  event handler. This is not the GENET IRQ13 parent interrupt clear path.

Important:
  - Writes to b6001818 are DQM queue/event W1C-style acks.
  - This function does not touch {@symbol 14e00048}
    or {@symbol 14e0004c}.
  - FPM endpoint writes are token/data return paths, not GENET TDMA descriptor
    writes.

