function: Plate comment @803e3230:
Flash subsystem detection and region-placement initializer candidate.

Behavior:
  - if global init latch at {@address 8147a44c} is already set, returns 1
  - clears flash region/runtime state at {@address 818ca920}, length 0x78
  - creates a mutex/semaphore and stores it at {@address 8147a46c}
  - attempts flash device 0 detection in this order:
      1. SPI flash:
          {@symbol 806109d8}
          {@symbol 80610a84}
          cleanup through {@symbol 80610a28}
      2. NAND flash:
          factory/init path through {@symbol 80515ed4}
          detect/build path through {@symbol 80515f80}
          cleanup through {@symbol 80515f24}
      3. memory-window flash device 0:
          memory-window query through {@symbol 803e5394}
          factory/init path through {@symbol 80195774}
          detect/build path through {@symbol 80195820}
          cleanup through {@symbol 801957c4}
  - validates flash device 0 size against the retrieved memory window
  - attempts flash device 1 detection if needed:
      NAND or memory-window flash depending on previous state
  - validates flash device 1:
      size must fit its memory window
      size must match flash device 0
      combined/dual-device sanity checks are applied
  - places detected flash regions through {@symbol 803e5854}
  - on failure, destroys any allocated flash device objects and clears global pointers
  - on success, computes a clamped runtime size/limit at {@address 8147a490}
      lower clamp: 0x10000
      upper clamp: 0x40000
  - sets global init latch at {@address 8147a44c}
  - returns 1 on success, 0 on failure

Current interpretation:
  This is the top-level flash subsystem initializer. It connects the SPI flash
  JEDEC path, NAND path, memory-window fallback path, device validation, and
  region-placement stage.

Keep _candidate:
  Overall role is clear, but several NAND/memory-window helper names and
  global field meanings are still provisional.

