function: BCM34xx serial/register 32-bit write helper.

Arguments:
  register_index = BCM34xx register index/address byte
  value = 32-bit value written through the serial command path

Behavior:
  - logs "Writing 0x%08x to 3410 register 0x%02x"
  - enters a recursive/owned serial-access lock rooted at
    {@symbol g_bcm34xx_serial_access_lock_ptr_8173EE0C_candidate}
  - if the current Stage1 context already owns the lock, increments the
    recursion count and continues
  - otherwise disables CP0 interrupt enable, waits on the embedded semaphore
    if another owner is active, then records the current context as owner
  - writes control/default word from
    {@symbol g_bcm3422_serial_ctrl_default_8173F8F0_candidate}
    to {@address b4e00e00}
  - writes register_index >> 2 to {@address b4e00e04}
  - splits value into four byte-wide words:
      low8       -> {@address b4e00e08}
      bits 15:8  -> {@address b4e00e0c}
      bits 23:16 -> {@address b4e00e10}
      bits 31:24 -> {@address b4e00e14}
  - writes transfer length 5 to {@address b4e00e24}
  - writes opcode 0xa0 to {@address b4e00e28}
  - writes 0 then 1 to {@address b4e00e2c}
  - polls {@address b4e00e2c} bit 0x02, yielding through
    {@symbol 8003d04c}
  - clears {@address b4e00e2c} after completion
  - releases the recursive/owned serial lock and posts the embedded semaphore
    if waiters exist

Current interpretation:
  BCM34xx/BCM3422 serial-access write32 path.

Important:
  This helper is not the PeriphIrq mask/status bank.
  It does not touch {@address b4e00048} or {@address b4e0004c}.
  It is not the GENET IRQ13 parent clear path.

